        "id": 230883,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-07-22T00:00:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ah, looks like some of the cards in your \"Meanwhile\" slots still activate abilities - they're not just cooling down. So you have to make sure you have enough movement between your currently selected card and your \"Meanwhile\" cards to do what you want... Though I don't see too many recurring movement abilities.</p>\n<p>Interesting, so you kind of build an ever-changing set of capabilities for your character, if I understand that right! And you might prefer to have certain cards out on your \"Meanwhile\" track *instead* of selected or in your hand ready to play, because of whatever buffs/abilities they give you while out in one of those slots. Seems like making a move-attack-move-attack-move-attack build for Tachyon is well within the reason of possibility.</p>\n<p>And the threats are doing the same thing - so that's kind of a way to have automated opponents act as if they're slowly changing their priorities, while maintaining some consistency over a few turns.</p>",
        "post_number": 71,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:05:59.923Z",
